# The uxn lane's core invariant is that a .rom is a PINNED, hash-then-execute artifact:
# byte-identical on x86, ARM and the phone, so the same ROM computes the same digit
# everywhere and a sha1 pin (mesh-rom-gate, mesh-rom-calibrate, mesh-log-attest's
# fletcher16, permcheck) means what it says. That identity was, until now, protected only
# by git's CONTENT heuristic — a .rom happened to look binary enough that autocrlf never
# mangled it. Heuristic, not contract. `binary` makes it explicit: no EOL conversion, no
# textconv, on every node regardless of core.autocrlf or a parent `* text=auto`. A .rom
# that gained a CRLF on one node's checkout would break its own sha1 — the one thing the
# whole fixed-point arc rests on. (Landed uxn-USE iter-4; test-rom-binary-contract gates it.)
*.rom binary

# The symbol table and the source ARE text — keep them diffable; a .rom.sym / .tal that
# stopped diffing would hide exactly the drift test-<name>'s rom==source check exists to catch.
*.rom.sym text
*.tal text
